# Git and worktree safety

## Preflight (before any edit)

Capture and keep: repository path, branch, `git rev-parse HEAD`,
`git status --porcelain`, `git worktree list`, remotes.

The task worktree must match the instructed branch/HEAD unless the current
human instruction says otherwise. If it does not, **stop without mutation**.

## Isolation

- One bounded task per branch/worktree.
- No unrelated edits.
- User changes are never discarded or overwritten.
- Parallel windows use disjoint path ownership from the worktree matrix.

## Forbidden unless the current human instruction explicitly authorizes it

- Destructive Git: `reset --hard`, `clean -fd`, force checkout, history rewrite
- Merge, rebase, cherry-pick (integration tasks must name this skill/scope)
- Push, pull request creation
- Worktree add/remove outside an invoked `parallel-worktree-wave` /
  `integration-gate` procedure

Stash, restore, or checkout that would drop user work is forbidden.

## Commit and push

- Local commit only when the current human instruction requests it.
- No push and no PR unless that instruction explicitly authorizes it.
- Do not skip hooks.

## Close-out

- Verify the task-owned tree is clean (unrelated pre-existing user files may
  remain only if they were recorded at preflight and were not touched).
- Report exact HEAD SHA and `git diff` / `git show` evidence for the commit.
